-- title:
--   Fibres of the level ring as base changes: étaleness and rank
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $f$, an element $u$ of the ring $A =$ `Afin p`, namely the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra `chartAlg` of the full modular function field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions at level $p$) determined over $\mathbb{Z}$ by the element `jFull p`, and a polynomial $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$. Let $P$ be a prime ideal of $R = \mathbb{Z}[1/f]$, realised as `Localization.Away f`, with residue field $\kappa(P)$, and let $k$ be a field equipped with a ring homomorphism $k \to \kappa(P)$. Write $B =$ `levelRing p f u g` for the quotient of $A[1/f] =$ `AfinAway p f` (the localisation of $A$ away from the image of $f$) by the principal ideal generated by $g$ evaluated at the image of $u$, and let $P.\mathrm{Fiber}\,B$ denote the fibre of $B$ at $P$, i.e. its base change to $\kappa(P)$. Put $Q_k = (k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A)/(1 \otimes g(u))$. The assertion is twofold: first, if $Q_k$ is étale over $k$, then $P.\mathrm{Fiber}\,B$ is étale over $\kappa(P)$; second, unconditionally, $\dim_{\kappa(P)} P.\mathrm{Fiber}\,B = \dim_k Q_k$. The étaleness part is an implication within the conclusion, not a standing hypothesis.
--
--   This is the fibrewise transfer step for the integral two-chart model of the modular curve: the fibre of the level ring $A[1/f]/(g(u))$ over a prime of $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$ is a base change of the fixed model $(k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A)/(1 \otimes g(u))$, so étaleness over the base field and the rank as a module over it are both inherited. It is used by [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin) and [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.rankAtStalk_levelRing_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.rankAtStalk_levelRing_eq).
